{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useQueuer<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): ReactQueuer<TValue, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/queuer/useQueuer.ts#L194","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queuer/useQueuer.ts:194"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A React hook that creates and manages a Queuer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a lower-level hook that provides direct access to the Queuer's functionality without\nany built-in state management. This allows you to integrate it with any state management solution\nyou prefer (useState, Redux, Zustand, etc.) by utilizing the onItemsChange callback."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a hook with built-in state management, see useQueuedState."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Queuer extends the base Queue to add processing capabilities. Items are processed\nsynchronously in order, with optional delays between processing each item. The queuer includes\nan internal tick mechanism that can be started and stopped, making it useful as a scheduler.\nWhen started, it will process one item per tick, with an optional wait time between ticks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default uses FIFO (First In First Out) behavior, but can be configured for LIFO\n(Last In First Out) by specifying 'front' position when adding items."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queuer.Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of items that have been processed by the queuer"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expirationCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of items that have been removed due to expiration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isEmpty"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the queuer has no items to process"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFull"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the queuer has reached its maximum capacity"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isIdle"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the queuer is not currently processing any items"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRunning"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the queuer is active and will process items automatically"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":": Array of items currently waiting to be processed"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"itemTimestamps"},{"type":"text","value":": Timestamps when items were added for expiration tracking"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingTick"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the queuer has a pending timeout for processing the next item"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rejectionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of items that have been rejected from being added"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of items currently in the queue"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current processing status ('idle' | 'running' | 'stopped')"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"unmount-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmount behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the hook stops the queuer when the component unmounts.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending items instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queue = useQueuer(fn, {\n  started: true,\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (q) => q.flush()\n});","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactQueuerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactQueuerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactQueuer.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactQueuer"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<queue.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ size: state.size, isRunning: state.isRunning })}>\n  {({ size, isRunning }) => (\n    <div>Queue: {size} items, {isRunning ? 'Processing' : 'Idle'}</div>\n  )}\n</queue.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when queue size changes at hook level (optimized for displaying queue length)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    size: state.size,\n    isEmpty: state.isEmpty,\n    isFull: state.isFull\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when processing state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isRunning: state.isRunning,\n    isIdle: state.isIdle,\n    status: state.status,\n    pendingTick: state.pendingTick\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution metrics change (optimized for stats display)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    executionCount: state.executionCount,\n    expirationCount: state.expirationCount,\n    rejectionCount: state.rejectionCount\n  })\n);\n\n// Example with custom state management and scheduling\nconst [items, setItems] = useState([]);\n\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  {\n    started: true, // Start processing immediately\n    wait: 1000,    // Process one item every second\n    onItemsChange: (queue) => setItems(queue.peekAllItems()),\n    getPriority: (item) => item.priority // Process higher priority items first\n  }\n);\n\n// Add items to process - they'll be handled automatically\nqueue.addItem('task1');\nqueue.addItem('task2');\n\n// Control the scheduler\nqueue.stop();  // Pause processing\nqueue.start(); // Resume processing\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { size, isRunning, executionCount } = queue.state;","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"unmount-behavior","text":"Unmount behavior","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useQueuer<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): ReactQueuer<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [queuer/useQueuer.ts:194](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/queuer/useQueuer.ts#L194)\n\nA React hook that creates and manages a Queuer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level hook that provides direct access to the Queuer's functionality without\nany built-in state management. This allows you to integrate it with any state management solution\nyou prefer (useState, Redux, Zustand, etc.) by utilizing the onItemsChange callback.\n\nFor a hook with built-in state management, see useQueuedState.\n\nThe Queuer extends the base Queue to add processing capabilities. Items are processed\nsynchronously in order, with optional delays between processing each item. The queuer includes\nan internal tick mechanism that can be started and stopped, making it useful as a scheduler.\nWhen started, it will process one item per tick, with an optional wait time between ticks.\n\nBy default uses FIFO (First In First Out) behavior, but can be configured for LIFO\n(Last In First Out) by specifying 'front' position when adding items.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:\n\n**1. Using `queuer.Subscribe` HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)**\n\nUse the `Subscribe` HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components.\n\n**2. Using the `selector` parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)**\n\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the `Subscribe` HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of items that have been processed by the queuer\n- `expirationCount`: Number of items that have been removed due to expiration\n- `isEmpty`: Whether the queuer has no items to process\n- `isFull`: Whether the queuer has reached its maximum capacity\n- `isIdle`: Whether the queuer is not currently processing any items\n- `isRunning`: Whether the queuer is active and will process items automatically\n- `items`: Array of items currently waiting to be processed\n- `itemTimestamps`: Timestamps when items were added for expiration tracking\n- `pendingTick`: Whether the queuer has a pending timeout for processing the next item\n- `rejectionCount`: Number of items that have been rejected from being added\n- `size`: Number of items currently in the queue\n- `status`: Current processing status ('idle' | 'running' | 'stopped')\n\n## Unmount behavior\n\nBy default, the hook stops the queuer when the component unmounts.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending items instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst queue = useQueuer(fn, {\n  started: true,\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (q) => q.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`item`) => `void`\n\n### options?\n\n[`ReactQueuerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactQueuerOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\> = `{}`\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ReactQueuer`](../interfaces/ReactQueuer.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<queue.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ size: state.size, isRunning: state.isRunning })}>\n  {({ size, isRunning }) => (\n    <div>Queue: {size} items, {isRunning ? 'Processing' : 'Idle'}</div>\n  )}\n</queue.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when queue size changes at hook level (optimized for displaying queue length)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    size: state.size,\n    isEmpty: state.isEmpty,\n    isFull: state.isFull\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when processing state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isRunning: state.isRunning,\n    isIdle: state.isIdle,\n    status: state.status,\n    pendingTick: state.pendingTick\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution metrics change (optimized for stats display)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    executionCount: state.executionCount,\n    expirationCount: state.expirationCount,\n    rejectionCount: state.rejectionCount\n  })\n);\n\n// Example with custom state management and scheduling\nconst [items, setItems] = useState([]);\n\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  {\n    started: true, // Start processing immediately\n    wait: 1000,    // Process one item every second\n    onItemsChange: (queue) => setItems(queue.peekAllItems()),\n    getPriority: (item) => item.priority // Process higher priority items first\n  }\n);\n\n// Add items to process - they'll be handled automatically\nqueue.addItem('task1');\nqueue.addItem('task2');\n\n// Control the scheduler\nqueue.stop();  // Pause processing\nqueue.start(); // Resume processing\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { size, isRunning, executionCount } = queue.state;\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useQueuer\ntitle: useQueuer\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useQueuer<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): ReactQueuer<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [queuer/useQueuer.ts:194](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/react-pacer/src/queuer/useQueuer.ts#L194)\n\nA React hook that creates and manages a Queuer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level hook that provides direct access to the Queuer's functionality without\nany built-in state management. This allows you to integrate it with any state management solution\nyou prefer (useState, Redux, Zustand, etc.) by utilizing the onItemsChange callback.\n\nFor a hook with built-in state management, see useQueuedState.\n\nThe Queuer extends the base Queue to add processing capabilities. Items are processed\nsynchronously in order, with optional delays between processing each item. The queuer includes\nan internal tick mechanism that can be started and stopped, making it useful as a scheduler.\nWhen started, it will process one item per tick, with an optional wait time between ticks.\n\nBy default uses FIFO (First In First Out) behavior, but can be configured for LIFO\n(Last In First Out) by specifying 'front' position when adding items.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe hook uses TanStack Store for reactive state management. You can subscribe to state changes\nin two ways:\n\n**1. Using `queuer.Subscribe` HOC (Recommended for component tree subscriptions)**\n\nUse the `Subscribe` HOC to subscribe to state changes deep in your component tree without\nneeding to pass a selector to the hook. This is ideal when you want to subscribe to state\nin child components.\n\n**2. Using the `selector` parameter (For hook-level subscriptions)**\n\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger a re-render\nat the hook level, optimizing performance by preventing unnecessary re-renders when irrelevant\nstate changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function or using the `Subscribe` HOC. This prevents unnecessary\nre-renders and gives you full control over when your component updates.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `executionCount`: Number of items that have been processed by the queuer\n- `expirationCount`: Number of items that have been removed due to expiration\n- `isEmpty`: Whether the queuer has no items to process\n- `isFull`: Whether the queuer has reached its maximum capacity\n- `isIdle`: Whether the queuer is not currently processing any items\n- `isRunning`: Whether the queuer is active and will process items automatically\n- `items`: Array of items currently waiting to be processed\n- `itemTimestamps`: Timestamps when items were added for expiration tracking\n- `pendingTick`: Whether the queuer has a pending timeout for processing the next item\n- `rejectionCount`: Number of items that have been rejected from being added\n- `size`: Number of items currently in the queue\n- `status`: Current processing status ('idle' | 'running' | 'stopped')\n\n## Unmount behavior\n\nBy default, the hook stops the queuer when the component unmounts.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending items instead:\n\n```tsx\nconst queue = useQueuer(fn, {\n  started: true,\n  wait: 1000,\n  onUnmount: (q) => q.flush()\n});\n```\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`item`) => `void`\n\n### options?\n\n[`ReactQueuerOptions`](../interfaces/ReactQueuerOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\> = `{}`\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ReactQueuer`](../interfaces/ReactQueuer.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// Subscribe to state changes deep in component tree using Subscribe HOC\n<queue.Subscribe selector={(state) => ({ size: state.size, isRunning: state.isRunning })}>\n  {({ size, isRunning }) => (\n    <div>Queue: {size} items, {isRunning ? 'Processing' : 'Idle'}</div>\n  )}\n</queue.Subscribe>\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when queue size changes at hook level (optimized for displaying queue length)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    size: state.size,\n    isEmpty: state.isEmpty,\n    isFull: state.isFull\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when processing state changes (optimized for loading indicators)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    isRunning: state.isRunning,\n    isIdle: state.isIdle,\n    status: state.status,\n    pendingTick: state.pendingTick\n  })\n);\n\n// Opt-in to re-render when execution metrics change (optimized for stats display)\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({\n    executionCount: state.executionCount,\n    expirationCount: state.expirationCount,\n    rejectionCount: state.rejectionCount\n  })\n);\n\n// Example with custom state management and scheduling\nconst [items, setItems] = useState([]);\n\nconst queue = useQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  {\n    started: true, // Start processing immediately\n    wait: 1000,    // Process one item every second\n    onItemsChange: (queue) => setItems(queue.peekAllItems()),\n    getPriority: (item) => item.priority // Process higher priority items first\n  }\n);\n\n// Add items to process - they'll be handled automatically\nqueue.addItem('task1');\nqueue.addItem('task2');\n\n// Control the scheduler\nqueue.stop();  // Pause processing\nqueue.start(); // Resume processing\n\n// Access the selected state (will be empty object {} unless selector provided)\nconst { size, isRunning, executionCount } = queue.state;\n```\n"}
